From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qcom_cpufreq_hw: the CPU's own pcpu, so the driver attaches

0041 checked cpu_get_pcpu(parent) in identify and cpu_get_pcpu of the
cpu device in probe. cpu_get_pcpu(dev) reads the pcpu from dev's parent,
so both asked cpulist, which has none for anyone: no CPU got its
frequency driver, powerd did not start, and the phone ran at the clock
Linux left (2026-11-01). Identify takes pcpu_find of the cpu's unit, as
ofw_cpu does when the MPIDR does not match (the boot CPU's is not set
with kern.smp.disabled); probe asks cpu_get_pcpu of its own device.

---
diff --git a/sys/arm64/qualcomm/qcom_cpufreq_hw.c b/sys/arm64/qualcomm/qcom_cpufreq_hw.c
index 36b5eca..f83ea5d 100644
--- a/sys/arm64/qualcomm/qcom_cpufreq_hw.c
+++ b/sys/arm64/qualcomm/qcom_cpufreq_hw.c
@@ -102,9 +102,11 @@ qcom_cpufreq_identify(driver_t *driver, device_t parent)
 	 * Only CPUs that run: ofw_cpu makes a cpu(4) for every CPU node, also
 	 * for those that were not started (kern.smp.disabled), and cpufreq(4)
 	 * dereferences their missing pcpu in its attach (a fatal data abort at
-	 * the boot on the phone, 2026-11-01).
+	 * the boot on the phone, 2026-11-01). Not cpu_get_pcpu(parent): that
+	 * asks parent's own parent, cpulist, which has no pcpu for anyone, so
+	 * no CPU had a frequency driver. ofw_cpu takes the unit's pcpu.
 	 */
-	if (cpu_get_pcpu(parent) == NULL)
+	if (pcpu_find(device_get_unit(parent)) == NULL)
 		return;
 	if (device_find_child(parent, "qcom_cpufreq", DEVICE_UNIT_ANY) != NULL)
 		return;
@@ -120,8 +122,7 @@ qcom_cpufreq_probe(device_t dev)
 	u_int domain;
 
 	if (qcom_cpufreq_domain(ofw_bus_get_node(device_get_parent(dev)),
-	    &provider, &domain) != 0 ||
-	    cpu_get_pcpu(device_get_parent(dev)) == NULL)
+	    &provider, &domain) != 0 || cpu_get_pcpu(dev) == NULL)
 		return (ENXIO);
 	device_set_desc(dev, "Qualcomm CPU frequency hardware");
 	return (BUS_PROBE_DEFAULT);
